WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.124
Hi, I'm Carillon!

00:00:02.124 --> 00:00:05.181
When a pager goes off, someone has to work out why.

00:00:05.181 --> 00:00:07.127
Datadog trained a model to do that.

00:00:09.683 --> 00:00:11.705
Real incidents have no clean labels.

00:00:11.705 --> 00:00:15.749
So simulate the system, inject a fault, and the fault you injected

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.097
is the answer key.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:21.340
Their simulator builds each training incident in four moves.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.661
An agent turns a real postmortem into a blueprint of the causal chain.

00:00:26.081 --> 00:00:30.374
Another agent builds a working system from it, or writes the telemetry directly.

00:00:30.794 --> 00:00:33.160
The fault is injected, and an alert fires.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.653
It is kept only if solvable, leak-free, and still hard.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.914
The model gets the alert and tries the same incident several times.

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:45.846
Each try queries a sandboxed copy of the real production tools.

00:00:46.266 --> 00:00:50.473
The diagnosis is scored for being right, and for claims the evidence supports.

00:00:50.893 --> 00:00:53.985
Tries are compared within the group, and new weights flow back

00:00:53.985 --> 00:00:55.110
as rollouts keep running.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.306
Training on the evaluation judge alone backfired.

00:00:59.306 --> 00:01:01.369
The model learned to claim less.

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:05.735
The reward that worked pays for chasing evidence, then for supported claims.

00:01:07.758 --> 00:01:10.915
On their internal benchmark, quality is plotted against cost.

00:01:11.335 --> 00:01:14.710
Scout at its highest effort matches Claude Fable five point one at

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:17.522
its highest effort, at about a quarter of the cost.

00:01:18.758 --> 00:01:22.378
On the public SREGym benchmark, Scout climbs into the top group.

00:01:22.378 --> 00:01:25.011
With one attempt per fault, those rows tie.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:30.586
Make the injected fault the label, train in the real harness, and

00:01:30.586 --> 00:01:32.765
never train on your evaluation judge alone.

00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:39.948
To recap: injected faults as labels, sandboxed real tools, and a reward

00:01:39.948 --> 00:01:41.436
that pays for evidence.

00:01:41.856 --> 00:01:44.009
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:44.624
I'm Carillon.

00:01:44.624 --> 00:01:44.932
Bye!
